+# Consulting Playbooks
+
+This directory contains the reusable consulting operating assets for the Young Consultations consulting practice. These assets were migrated from Young-Consultations/slugger in August 2026, establishing `consulting-playbook` as the authoritative home for all reusable consulting operating content.
+
+## Standard Engagement Lifecycle
+
+Lead → Qualification → Discovery → Engagement Scope → Evidence Collection → Interviews → Assessment → Findings → Recommendations → 30/60/90 Roadmap → Leadership Readout → Implementation Proposal → Closeout
+
+## Directory Structure
+
+| Directory | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| [service/](service/) | Service offer definitions and scope templates |
+| [engagement/intake/](engagement/intake/) | Client qualification checklist, intake questionnaire, engagement readiness checklist |
+| [engagement/discovery/](engagement/discovery/) | Discovery call agenda, stakeholder interview guide, interview notes template |
+| [assessment/checklists/](assessment/checklists/) | Backlog health, sprint health, SDLC maturity, AI-SDLC readiness, and software delivery assessment checklists |
+| [assessment/evidence/](assessment/evidence/) | Evidence request list, evidence inventory template, evidence traceability matrix |
+| [assessment/findings/](assessment/findings/) | Finding template, recommendation template, prioritization matrix, risk register, assessment scorecard |
+| [reporting/](reporting/) | Executive assessment report, executive summary template, leadership readout outline |
+| [roadmap/](roadmap/) | 30/60/90-day roadmap, implementation backlog template, definition-of-done template |
+| [proposals/](proposals/) | Consulting proposal template, statement-of-work template, change-request template, engagement closeout checklist |
+| [case-studies/](case-studies/) | Reusable case study template and Slugger internal case study outline |
+| [knowledge/](knowledge/) | Consulting principles, definitions and glossary, reusable prompts, lessons-learned template |
+
+## Operating Principles
+
+- Customer value drives prioritization.
+- Evidence must support findings.
+- Observations, conclusions, and recommendations must remain distinct.
+- Every finding must include customer or business impact.
+- Every recommendation must include an owner and measurable definition of done.
+- AI-generated content must be human-reviewed.
+- Client confidentiality and intellectual property must be protected.
+- Slugger may assist the workflow as a tool but does not replace accountable human judgment.
+
+## Ownership
+
+These assets are owned and maintained by `Young-Consultations/consulting-playbook`. Slugger (`Young-Consultations/slugger`) is an AI-assisted software-development orchestration product that may be used as a tool during consulting engagements, but consulting operating assets are not part of the Slugger product.
